===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|Welch||archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|Walsch}}, {{m|enm|Welische}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wīelisċ||Briton; Roman; Celt}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*walhisk}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*walhiskaz||Celt; later Roman}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*walhaz||Celt, Roman}} (compare {{cog|ang|wealh}}), from the name of the {{der|en|cel-gau|-}} tribe, the {{w|Volcae}} (recorded only in Latin contexts).

This word was borrowed from Germanic into Slavic (compare {{cog|cu|Влахъ||Vlachs, Romanians}}, {{cog|gkm|Βλάχος}}).

{{doublet|en|Vellish}}. Compare {{m|en|Walloon}}, {{m|en|walnut}}, {{m|en|Vlach}}, {{m|en|Walach}}, {{m|en|Gaul}}, {{m|en|Cornwall}}.

